/target
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock is committed — this is a binary project, reproducible builds
# require the lock (prev practice of gitignoring it produced divergent CI
# builds vs local builds).
.env
.env.local
*.log
.DS_Store
data/
node_data/
logs/
*.sqlite
*.db

# Archive / releases (não versionar)
docs/*.tar.gz
docs/*.tar
*.bak
*.tmp
scan/node_modules/
scan/dist/
scan/.astro/
loc-alpha.txt
loc-beta-day0.txt

# Rollback packages are BUILD OUTPUT, never the store of record
# (deploy/RELEASE-INTEGRITY.md §5.2) — and the .key next to a generated
# package is a signing secret, which must never reach GitLab or GitHub.
deploy/rollback/dist/
*.minisign.key
rollback-signing.key

# Image-signing / TLS private key material (Round-1 finding MED-11):
# cosign.key is the root of trust for deploy/attestation/image-security-
# policy.json and, through it, the SEV-SNP HOSTDATA binding — a private key
# created by a convenience `cosign generate-key-pair` run in the repo and
# swept up by `git add -A` is a signing key nobody decided to publish. Same
# reasoning as bench/ above for BPOSKEY1: this is prevention, not cleanup.
cosign.key
*.pem
*.p12

# Personal session journal (not versioned)
journal.txt

# Tauri desktop build artifacts
desktop/src-tauri/target/
desktop/src-tauri/gen/

# build artifacts in any subcrate
**/target/
carryover.tsv

# PDF gerado a partir do .md pelo pipeline do spike — nao versionar
docs/specs/*.pdf

# Worktrees de agentes: repos git embutidos, nunca conteudo do projeto.
.claude/worktrees/
deploy/artifacts/

# Orquestracao local de agentes: nao e artefato do protocolo.
.claude/

# Python bytecode (sdk/codegen, tools/*)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Fixtures de benchmark. Contem `validator.key` de descarte — chave privada NAO
# entra no repositorio, nem descartavel: este repo e empurrado para GitLab e
# GitHub, e uma chave commitada e indistinguivel de um vazamento para quem
# audita depois. Regenerar com os scripts de bench.
#
# Isto e prevencao, nao limpeza: em 01/09/2026 um levantamento achou 41
# `BPOSKEY1` numa branch de trabalho, e o commit que as adiciona e ANCESTRAL de
# duas outras — apagar a branch de origem nao as remove. Aquelas duas so podem
# ser cherry-picked, nunca mescladas.
bench/

# SP1 guest build artifact (cargo prove build) — bake the vkey, not the ELF
crates/coherence-prover/program/elf/

# LOW-6 (Round 1): the blanket `*.log` and `.claude/` rules above have
# force-added tracked members — `git status` was blind to edits-by-deletion
# in these paths, and a new file added there was silently ignored instead of
# staged. Explicit negations, not a directory-wide re-inclusion, so nothing
# else under `.claude/` (agent scratch state, not project content) comes
# back. (os/boot-harness/fixtures/ ALSO carries its own nested .gitignore
# with `!*.log` for the same reason — this negation is the belt to that
# suspenders, matching what `git ls-files` shows is actually tracked there.)
!os/boot-harness/fixtures/*.log
!.claude/workflows/
